{"slug": "plum-and-mozzarella-salad-with-serrano-lime-dressing", "nyt_id": 783530839, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/783530839-plum-and-mozzarella-salad-with-serrano-lime-dressing", "name": "Plum and Mozzarella Salad With Serrano-Lime Dressing", "author": "Ashley Lonsdale", "description": "This is a simple salad for when time is scarce but flavor aspirations are high. Sliced ripe plums and milky mozzarella produce a fresh, cooling and minimalist dish, perfect for hot summer evenings. When assembling salads that have few major ingredients, like this one, consider layering dressing elements to create more dimension. For instance, the lime juice and red wine vinegar add multiple bright notes to the spicy serrano dressing. Similarly, honey echoes and amplifies the plum's sweetness. The salad can stand on its own as a light meal but also does well with good toast or alongside an equally straightforward shrimp recipe.", "servings": {"text": "4-6 servings", "min": 4, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 20, "cook_minutes": 5, "total_minutes": 25, "raw": {"total": "25 min", "prep": "PT0H20M", "cook": "PT0H5M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 tablespoons fresh lime juice (from 1 lime)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "fresh lime juice (from 1 lime)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 tablespoons red wine vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "red wine vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 tablespoons honey", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "honey", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 fresh serrano chile, thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "fresh serrano chile", "preparation": "thinly sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, 